{"parentUuid":"c3aad1ad-975e-4250-8bab-950aef6895bf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"ae0d80dfdeb39ff29","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Az94Kao987knLc6i4FxjDZ","type":"tool_result","content":"##### security-engineering cross-cutting ['all'] runtime= False\nP: Threat modeling and trust boundaries for every untrusted input, secure-coding and memory-safety policy, supply-chain security, secrets, anti-tamper boundary, privacy engineering, mod/UGC sandbox policy.\nNR: [['Cheat detection', 'anti-cheat-integrity'], ['Fuzzing campaigns', 'robustness-fuzzing'], ['Transport encryption implementation', 'network-transport']]\nprov ['C-TRUST'] cons []\n{}\n##### observability-telemetry cross-cutting ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Instrumentation substrate: structured logging, trace zones (CPU, GPU, IO, memory), counters and metrics, profiler integrations, in-game stats, development and live telemetry with privacy consent; zero cost when compiled out.\nNR: [['Crash capture', 'crash-diagnostics'], ['Debug drawing and consoles', 'visual-debugging-tools'], ['Perf budgets', 'performance-architect']]\nprov ['C-INSTR'] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### crash-diagnostics cross-cutting ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Crash, hang and GPU-fault capture and reporting: minidumps, symbolication, bucketing and triage, GPU crash dumps, watchdogs, OOM reports, assert reporting.\nNR: [['Emitting GPU breadcrumbs', 'rhi-core'], ['Symbol server infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\nprov ['C-CRASH'] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-INSTR']\n{}\n##### determinism-replay cross-cutting ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Defines determinism levels (none, same-binary, cross-platform) per subsystem and the floating-point and parallel-execution rules that achieve them; owns input/state record-replay and desync detection.\nNR: [['Rollback netcode', 'prediction-rollback'], ['Deterministic math implementation', 'math-simd-numerics']]\nprov ['C-DET'] cons ['C-MATH', 'C-TASK', 'C-SER']\n{}\n##### hot-reload-iteration cross-cutting ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Owns the reload protocol (change detection, dependency invalidation, state preservation) that assets, shaders, scripts, config and C++ live coding plug into; measures edit → see latency.\nNR: [[\"Each system's own reload implementation\", 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Build system', 'build-system-toolchains']]\nprov ['C-RELOAD'] cons ['C-RES', 'C-MOD', 'C-REFL']\n{}\n##### ml-inference-runtime expert ['aaa'] runtime= True\nP: Runtime neural-network inference shared by neural rendering, animation, audio and AI: GPU (cooperative-vector / tensor) and CPU backends, model packaging and quantization, scheduling within frame budgets, determinism characteristics.\nNR: [['Vendor upscalers', 'reconstruction-upscaling'], ['Neural feature design (texture, material, animation)', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\nprov ['C-ML'] cons ['C-RHI', 'C-RG', 'C-TASK']\n{}\n##### core-runtime-architect lead ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Core runtime architecture: layering within core, module system and engine lifecycle (parallel boot, init graph, shutdown), configuration and cvars, error-handling and failure model, language and compiler feature policy.\nNR: [['Allocator design', 'memory-allocators'], ['Scheduler', 'job-system-task-graph'], ['Frame loop', 'frame-orchestration']]\nprov ['C-MOD', 'C-CFG', 'C-ERR'] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### math-simd-numerics expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Math and numerics: SIMD linear algebra, geometry and intersection primitives, computational geometry, numerical robustness, mixed and double precision, deterministic math, RNG and noise, curves, quantized formats, SPMD kernels with ISA dispatch.\nNR: [['Coordinate conventions decision', 'engine-architect'], ['Determinism rules', 'determinism-replay']]\nprov ['C-MATH'] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### memory-allocators expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Memory management: virtual memory, allocator families, thread-local and NUMA-aware allocation, tagging and attribution, budget enforcement mechanisms, fragmentation control, memory debugging, OOM policy, UMA accounting.\nNR: [['GPU heaps', 'gpu-memory-resources'], ['Budget numbers', 'performance-architect']]\nprov ['C-MEM'] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### containers-core-types expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Containers and core types: cache-friendly containers (open-addressing maps, inline and SoA containers, rings), strings and UTF-8, interned names, hashing, bit utilities, algorithms, explicit-ownership and view types.\nNR: [['Concurrent containers', 'concurrency-primitives'], ['Entity handles', 'entity-object-model']]\nprov ['C-TYPES'] cons ['C-MEM']\n{}\n##### concurrency-primitives expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Memory model and atomics, synchronization primitives, lock-free and wait-free structures, safe memory reclamation, thread-safety annotations and model checking; reviewer for concurrent code engine-wide.\nNR: [['Scheduling', 'job-system-task-graph'], ['Concurrency test campaigns', 'robustness-fuzzing']]\nprov ['C-SYNC'] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### job-system-task-graph expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Task-parallel execution: work-stealing scheduler, dependency task graphs, fibers and C++20 coroutines, priorities and QoS, heterogeneous-core and NUMA placement, IO/GPU completion integration, parallel algorithms, blocking policy.\nNR: [['Frame phase layout', 'frame-orchestration'], ['IO backends', 'async-io-storage']]\nprov ['C-TASK'] cons ['C-SYNC', 'C-PAL']\n{}\n##### frame-orchestration expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: The engine loop expressed as a task graph: frame pipelining across simulation, render and GPU, tick phases and sync points, fixed-step simulation with interpolation, time domains, latency and pacing control.\nNR: [['System ordering inside a phase', 'ecs-runtime'], ['Swapchain presentation', 'rhi-core']]\nprov ['C-FRAME'] cons ['C-TASK', 'C-CFG']\n{}\n##### entity-object-model expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Object-model strategy and identity: generational entity IDs, stable GUIDs, hard/soft/weak references, the hybrid-model policy stating which data lives in ECS vs services vs asset objects vs UI, events and messaging.\nNR: [['ECS storage and queries', 'ecs-runtime'], ['Asset references', 'content-pipeline-architect'], ['Network IDs', 'replication']]\nprov ['C-ID'] cons ['C-TYPES', 'C-SYNC']\n{}\n##### ecs-runtime expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: ECS: storage (archetype chunks or sparse sets, chosen by ADR), queries, change detection, structural changes and command buffers, system scheduling with access-conflict analysis, relationships, singletons, authoring → runtime baking, debugging.\nNR: [['World partition', 'world-architect'], ['Transform propagation', 'spatial-transforms'], ['Object-model policy', 'entity-object-model']]\nprov ['C-ECS'] cons ['C-ID', 'C-TASK', 'C-FRAME', 'C-REFL?']\n{}\n##### reflection-metadata expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Type registry, reflection generation (codegen now, C++26 static reflection when toolchains allow), attributes, the property system, script-binding substrate, dynamic invocation.\nNR: [['Serialization formats', 'serialization-schema'], ['Editor widgets', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['Script VM', 'scripting-runtime']]\nprov ['C-REFL'] cons ['C-TYPES']\n{}\n##### serialization-schema expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Binary and text formats, schema evolution and upgraders, in-place loadable layouts, canonical deterministic serialization, portability, and validation of untrusted input.\nNR: [['Package containers', 'package-formats-vfs'], ['Network bit packing', 'replication'], ['Save-game semantics', 'persistence-save']]\nprov ['C-SER'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-TYPES']\n{}\n##### platform-architect lead ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Platform abstraction layer and porting strategy: OS services, CPU/GPU capability discovery, windowing, process lifecycle, capability tiers, and evaluation of new targets (web, cloud streaming).\nNR: [['Graphics API backends', 'rhi-core'], ['Store and online services', 'platform-online-services'], ['Toolchains', 'build-system-toolchains']]\nprov ['C-PAL'] cons []\n{}\n##### platform-desktop expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Windows, Linux, SteamOS and macOS integration: display modes, HDR and VRR capability, DPI, OS-specific IO and scheduling behavior, handheld-PC specifics, server host OS.\nNR: [['HDR signal encoding', 'post-color-hdr'], ['Swapchain', 'rhi-core']]\nprov [] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### platform-console expert ['std3d'] runtime= True\nP: Console-class integration from platform-holder documentation: OS and memory model (UMA), suspend/resume, multi-user model, devkit workflows, platform requirements feeding certification.\nNR: [['Certification tracking', 'certification-compliance'], ['Console graphics API backend', 'rhi-core']]\nprov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SVC']\n{}\n##### platform-mobile-portable expert ['mobile3d', 'min2d'] runtime= True\nP: iOS, Android and portable-console integration: app lifecycle, thermal and power adaptivity, tile-based GPU implications, storage and download-size constraints.\nNR: [['Render-graph TBDR optimizations', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Touch input', 'input-devices-haptics']]\nprov [] cons ['C-PAL']\n{}\n##### resource-streaming-architect lead ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Runtime resource model: handles and explicit lifetime, load requests with priority and deadline, dependency-aware loading, the streaming manager (budgets, eviction, prediction), fallbacks, no-stall loading.\nNR: [['IO backends', 'async-io-storage'], ['Package format', 'package-formats-vfs'], ['Texture-specific streaming', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\nprov ['C-RES'] cons ['C-ASSET', 'C-VFS', 'C-IO', 'C-TASK']\n{}\n##### async-io-storage expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Async IO: io_uring, IOCP, DirectStorage and console backends, IO scheduling and queue depth, GPU decompression, memory-mapped IO, file-system abstraction, error handling.\nNR: [['Streaming decisions', 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Codec choice', 'package-formats-vfs']]\nprov ['C-IO'] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-GPUMEM?']\n{}\n##### package-formats-vfs expert ['all'] runtime= True\nP: Package/container format and chunking, codec selection, VFS mount layering (base, patch, DLC, mods), encryption and signing, install-chunk layout.\nNR: [['Patch generation', 'packaging-release-patching'], ['Relocatable data layout', 'serialization-schema']]\nprov ['C-VFS'] cons ['C-IO', 'C-SER']\n{}\n##### rhi-core expert ['client'] runtime= True\nP: Render hardware interface over D3D12, Vulkan, Metal, console APIs and WebGPU: queues and command recording, synchronization, bindless descriptors, PSOs and PSO caching, presentation, capability tiers, GPU crash breadcrumbs, driver workarounds.\nNR: [['GPU memory allocation', 'gpu-memory-resources'], ['Barrier planning', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Shader compilation', 'shader-system']]\nprov ['C-RHI'] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-SYNC']\n{}\n##### gpu-memory-resources expert ['client'] runtime= True\nP: GPU heaps and suballocation, residency and overcommit, upload/readback rings, sparse/reserved resources, GPU memory budgeting and defragmentation, lifetimes decoupled from frame boundaries.\nNR: [['Transient aliasing plans', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Texture streaming policy', 'texture-streaming-vt']]\nprov ['C-GPUMEM'] cons ['C-RHI']\n{}\n##### render-graph-scheduling expert ['client'] runtime= True\nP: Render graph declaration and compilation, automatic barriers, transient aliasing, async compute and multi-queue scheduling, TBDR pass merging, history resources, work-graph integration, general GPU compute, readback contract.\nNR: [['Heap allocation', 'gpu-memory-resources'], ['Feature passes', 'render-architect']]\nprov ['C-RG'] cons ['C-RHI', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-TASK']\n{}\n##### texture-streaming-vt expert ['mobile3d', 'std3d'] runtime= True\nP: Runtime texture formats, mip streaming, sampler-feedback streaming, virtual texturing, streaming-friendly cooked layout; evaluates neural texture compression.\nNR: [['Texture encoding in cook', 'asset-cook-processors'], ['Streaming manager', 'resource-streaming-architect']]\nprov [] cons ['C-RES', 'C-GPUMEM', 'C-RG', 'C-COOK', 'C-ML?']\n{}\n##### audio-architect lead ['client'] runtime= True\nP: Audio engine architecture and threading, device backends, voice management and virtualization, middleware decision, audio budgets.\nNR: [['DSP algorithms', 'audio-dsp-mixing'], ['Spatialization', 'spatial-audio-acoustics']]\nprov ['C-AUDIO'] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-ECS', 'C-SPATIAL']\n{}\n##### editor-architect lead ['client'] runtime= False\nP: Editor architecture: process model (in- vs out-of-process runtime), editor/runtime data separation, transactions and undo/redo, selection, extension API and tool scripting, play-in-editor isolation, remote live editing, headless editor, large-project performance.\nNR: [['Panels and inspectors', 'editor-ui-framework'], ['World viewport tools', 'world-editor-viewport'], ['Source control', 'collaboration-version-control']]\nprov ['C-EDCMD'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-SER', 'C-ASSET', 'C-WORLD', 'C-PLUGIN', 'C-UI?']\n{}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"92eda15f-4dc7-42f9-866c-017da8d71f36","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:46:28.817Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c3aad1ad-975e-4250-8bab-950aef6895bf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
