{"parentUuid":"e139c989-20d9-42eb-8634-3c2f4bd176a0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"9bdfc07b-8ff1-4e95-9c88-de7440fd6192","agentId":"ae0d80dfdeb39ff29","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FMDVZLXBUMYC4RuHsyKP9H","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"_doc\": \"Every cross-cutting requirement from the brief has one owning skill that defines the obligation and reviews every other skill against it. 'obligation' is what each skill's SKILL.md must address in phase 2.\",\n  \"concerns\": [\n    {\"concern\": \"performance\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare budgets per tier, hot paths, and the benchmark that proves them.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"memory usage\", \"owner\": \"memory-allocators\", \"obligation\": \"Declare allocation strategy, memory tags, peak/steady budgets and OOM behavior.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"cache behavior\", \"owner\": \"cpu-performance\", \"obligation\": \"Declare data layouts of hot data and access patterns; justify pointer chasing.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"concurrency\", \"owner\": \"concurrency-primitives\", \"obligation\": \"Declare threading model, shared state, synchronization and task-graph placement.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"latency\", \"owner\": \"frame-orchestration\", \"obligation\": \"Declare frame phase placement and latency contribution.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"determinism\", \"owner\": \"determinism-replay\", \"obligation\": \"Declare the determinism level provided and how it is tested.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"observability\", \"owner\": \"observability-telemetry\", \"obligation\": \"Declare trace zones, counters and logs; zero cost when compiled out.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"debugging\", \"owner\": \"visual-debugging-tools\", \"obligation\": \"Declare debug visualizations, inspectors and console commands.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"testing\", \"owner\": \"test-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Meet the test definition of done (unit, contract, integration, fuzz where untrusted).\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"scalability\", \"owner\": \"performance-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare behavior from the smallest to the largest configuration and the scaling knobs.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"security\", \"owner\": \"security-engineering\", \"obligation\": \"Declare untrusted inputs and validation; follow the trust-boundary contract.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"platform portability\", \"owner\": \"platform-architect\", \"obligation\": \"No platform code above the PAL; declare capability-tier behavior.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"maintainability\", \"owner\": \"architecture-governance\", \"obligation\": \"Contracts documented, ADRs recorded, fitness functions pass.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"tooling\", \"owner\": \"editor-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Declare authoring path, inspectors and editor integration for every user-facing feature.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"failure recovery\", \"owner\": \"core-runtime-architect\", \"obligation\": \"Follow the error model; declare degradation and recovery behavior.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"hot reload\", \"owner\": \"hot-reload-iteration\", \"obligation\": \"Declare what reloads live and how state is preserved.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"data migration\", \"owner\": \"serialization-schema\", \"obligation\": \"Version every persisted format and ship upgraders.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"backwards compatibility\", \"owner\": \"api-lifecycle-migration\", \"obligation\": \"Classify APIs public/internal and follow deprecation policy.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"developer usability\", \"owner\": \"developer-experience-docs\", \"obligation\": \"Ship docs, a sample, and actionable error messages.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"accessibility\", \"owner\": \"accessibility\", \"obligation\": \"Map player-facing features to accessibility requirements.\"},\n    {\"concern\": \"evidence\", \"owner\": \"research-evidence\", \"obligation\": \"Every major decision cites graded evidence and a maturity class.\"}\n  ]\n}\nK-ARCH ['all', 'tier:orchestrator', 'research-evidence', 'subtree:api-lifecycle-migration', 'subtree:world-architect', 'developer-experience-docs'] ['every capability has exactly one owner and the owner is the right expertise', 'non-responsibilities point to the real owner', 'contracts are minimal, stable and layered', 'no hidden cyclic build dependencies', 'leads have real territory, not just coordination']\nK-RENDER ['subtree:render-architect', 'render-validation', 'gpu-performance', 'terrain', 'vegetation-foliage', 'water-ocean', 'atmosphere-weather', 'deformation-skinning', 'xr-runtime', 'ml-inference-runtime'] ['no draw-call-centric or DX11-era assumptions', 'render graph owns sync and aliasing', 'technique maturity labels are honest', 'scale-down path exists for each feature']\nK-SYSTEMS ['subtree:core-runtime-architect', 'subtree:resource-streaming-architect', 'observability-telemetry', 'crash-diagnostics', 'determinism-replay', 'hot-reload-iteration', 'rhi-core', 'gpu-memory-resources', 'render-graph-scheduling', 'audio-architect', 'network-transport', 'ml-inference-runtime', 'subtree:world-architect'] ['no single-thread-first assumptions', 'explicit ownership and lifetimes', 'synchronization minimized and justified', 'async IO end to end', 'heterogeneous cores and NUMA considered']\nK-SIM ['subtree:physics-architect', 'crowd-simulation', 'ik-procedural-animation', 'prediction-rollback', 'determinism-replay', 'procedural-generation', 'water-ocean', 'vfx-particles'] ['stepping and sync with frame phases are explicit', 'determinism levels are declared', 'simulation LOD exists for large scales', 'build-vs-integrate evidence']\nK-NET ['subtree:network-architect', 'anti-cheat-integrity', 'platform-online-services', 'destruction-fracture', 'persistence-save', 'packaging-release-patching'] ['netcode model matches game type', 'authority and trust explicit', 'bandwidth and scale budgets', 'version compatibility', 'service boundaries clear']\nK-TOOLS ['subtree:editor-architect', 'subtree:content-pipeline-architect', 'hot-reload-iteration', 'developer-experience-docs', 'ui-architect', 'terrain', 'procedural-generation', 'cinematics-sequencer', 'scripting-runtime', 'world-data-model', 'subtree:build-release-architect'] ['tooling as thorough as runtime', 'undo/transactions universal', 'large teams can collaborate without lock contention', 'iteration time measured', 'pipeline deterministic and cached']\nK-PLATFORM ['subtree:platform-architect', 'rhi-core', 'subtree:build-release-architect', 'certification-compliance', 'async-io-storage', 'crash-diagnostics'] ['PAL is the only platform-specific layer', 'console, mobile and web constraints represented', 'certification requirements traced', 'packaging and patching per platform']\nK-PERF ['all', 'subtree:performance-architect', 'subtree:world-architect'] ['budgets exist for each subsystem', 'benchmarks include realistic workloads', 'no hidden global sync points', 'asymptotics stated for world-scale data']\nK-PROD ['all', 'tier:orchestrator', 'developer-experience-docs', 'subtree:build-release-architect'] ['content creators are first-class', 'features have an owner through ship', 'live-ops and patching covered', 'scale-down keeps small teams productive']\nK-FUTURE ['all'] ['extension points exist for emerging techniques', 'maturity labels allow promotion', \"no hard-coding of today's API limits\"]\nK-COMPLETE ['all'] [\"compare against shipped engines' feature sets\", 'compare against platform requirements', 'compare against production pipelines end to end']\nK-LEGACY ['all'] ['each flagged pattern either absent or justified by an ADR']\nK-GAMEPLAY ['subtree:animation-architect', 'subtree:audio-architect', 'subtree:gameplay-architect', 'subtree:ui-architect', 'accessibility', 'input-system', 'input-devices-haptics', 'character-vehicle-physics'] ['designers and animators have authoring paths', 'accessibility and localization built in, not bolted on', 'gameplay extension points']\nK-QUALITY ['all', 'subtree:test-architect', 'subtree:security-engineering', 'subtree:api-lifecycle-migration'] ['each skill has objective validation', 'untrusted inputs fuzzed', 'determinism and concurrency tested', 'security boundaries explicit']\n{\"base\": {\"min2d\": \"Small 2D / 2.5D indie game\", \"mobile3d\": \"Mobile / portable 3D game\", \"std3d\": \"Modern 3D game on PC / console\", \"server\": \"Headless dedicated game server\"}, \"addons\": {\"openworld\": \"Large streamed worlds\", \"online\": \"Networked multiplayer\", \"aaa\": \"High-end AAA feature set\", \"xr\": \"VR / MR\", \"ugc\": \"Mods & user-generated content\"}}\n{\"indie-2d\": [\"min2d\"], \"indie-2d-online-moddable\": [\"min2d\", \"online\", \"ugc\"], \"mobile-3d\": [\"mobile3d\"], \"standard-3d\": [\"std3d\"], \"open-world\": [\"std3d\", \"openworld\"], \"online-3d\": [\"std3d\", \"online\"], \"aaa-open-world-online\": [\"std3d\", \"openworld\", \"online\", \"aaa\", \"ugc\"], \"dedicated-server\": [\"server\", \"online\"], \"xr-3d\": [\"std3d\", \"xr\"]}\n##### program-orchestration ['all']\nP: Turns architecture into coordinated multi-agent work: decomposes milestones into tasks by skill territory, keeps the ownership ledger and territory locks, sequences integration through vertical slices, routes contract change requests, and schedules critic gates.\nNR: [['Deciding architecture', 'engine-architect'], ['CI mechanics', 'ci-cd-automation'], ['Release versioning', 'build-release-architect']]\nprov ['C-ORCH'] cons []\n##### perf-benchmarking ['all']\nP: Benchmark harnesses (micro and representative-workload scenes), automated capture, statistical analysis (variance, significance), regression detection and bisection, dashboards.\nNR: [['Setting budgets', 'performance-architect'], ['CI infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\nprov [] cons ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET']\n##### cpu-performance ['all']\nP: CPU microarchitecture-level optimization and review: cache and memory-access patterns, vectorization audits, contention and false sharing, hybrid-core and power-aware tuning, PGO/LTO.\nNR: [['Owning subsystem code', 'engine-architect'], ['Math library', 'math-simd-numerics'], ['Scheduler design', 'job-system-task-graph']]\nprov [] cons ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET', 'C-TASK']\n##### loading-streaming-performance ['all']\nP: End-to-end load time, startup time and hitch elimination (PSO compilation, streaming stalls, GC pauses, synchronous waits), IO throughput analysis.\nNR: [['IO backend implementation', 'async-io-storage'], ['PSO cache implementation', 'rhi-core'], ['Streaming policy', 'resource-streaming-architect']]\nprov [] cons ['C-INSTR', 'C-BUDGET', 'C-IO', 'C-RES']\n##### functional-automation-soak ['all']\nP: Game-level automation: scripted and bot playthroughs, smoke/boot tests, soak and stability runs (memory growth, leaks), hardware/OS compatibility matrix, network harnesses and server load tests.\nNR: [['Unit test frameworks', 'test-architect'], ['Device-farm infrastructure', 'ci-cd-automation']]\nprov [] cons ['C-GAME?', 'C-INPUT?', 'C-NET?']\n##### robustness-fuzzing ['all']\nP: Robustness engineering: fuzzing every untrusted-input parser (assets, packets, saves, scripts, mods), sanitizer build policy, fault injection (IO errors, OOM, device lost), concurrency stress and schedule perturbation.\nNR: [['Threat model', 'security-engineering'], ['Fixing parsers', 'serialization-schema']]\nprov [] cons ['C-SER', 'C-IO']\n##### plugin-system ['all']\nP: Plugin architecture: manifests, discovery, dependency resolution, load phases, binary vs source plugins, isolation, distribution format.\nNR: [['Mods & UGC', 'modding-ugc'], ['Module linking internals', 'core-runtime-architect']]\nprov ['C-PLUGIN'] cons ['C-MOD']\n##### content-pipeline-architect ['all']\nP: Asset identity and the content pipeline: asset registry and dependency graph, deterministic incremental per-platform cooking, the cook-step contract, derived-data cache and content-addressed store, distributed cooking, content validation.\nNR: [['Format-specific builders (shaders, animation, clusters…)', 'shader-system'], ['Runtime loading', 'resource-streaming-architect'], ['Import formats', 'asset-import-interchange']]\nprov ['C-ASSET', 'C-COOK'] cons ['C-SER', 'C-TASK', 'C-REFL']\n##### world-architect ['all']\nP: World representation strategy (data-oriented, no universal scene graph), partitioning and streaming cells, streaming sources, HLOD strategy, simulation LOD and significance, large-world coordinate policy, level transitions, server-side world streaming.\nNR: [['World document format', 'world-data-model'], ['Transform math', 'spatial-transforms'], ['HLOD mesh generation', 'virtualized-geometry-lod']]\nprov ['C-WORLD'] cons ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-RES', 'C-ECS']\n##### spatial-transforms ['all']\nP: Transform representation and parallel hierarchy propagation, attachments, large-world coordinates implementation, generic spatial index and query service for non-physics consumers, spatial hashing.\nNR: [['Physics broadphase', 'collision-detection'], ['GPU culling', 'gpu-driven-pipeline']]\nprov ['C-SPATIAL'] cons ['C-MATH', 'C-ECS', 'C-TASK']\n##### render-architect ['client']\nP: Rendering architecture: pipeline organization, shading-path choice (forward+, deferred, visibility buffer), render-feature contract, render scene and world→render sync, scalability tiers from 2D mobile to path-traced, multi-view, debug modes, render threading.\nNR: [['API backends', 'rhi-core'], ['Pass scheduling', 'render-graph-scheduling'], ['Individual features (GI, shadows…)', 'global-illumination']]\nprov ['C-RSCENE'] cons ['C-RG', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-MATIF', 'C-FRAME', 'C-ECS']\n##### physics-architect ['all']\nP: Physics architecture: build vs integrate decision, physics world representation and ECS integration, stepping and frame sync, determinism levels, physics LOD, materials, GPU offload evaluation; covers both 2D and 3D.\nNR: [['Collision algorithms', 'collision-detection'], ['Solvers', 'rigid-body-dynamics'], ['Networked physics', 'prediction-rollback']]\nprov ['C-PHYS'] cons ['C-SPATIAL', 'C-ECS', 'C-FRAME', 'C-DET', 'C-TASK']\n##### animation-architect ['all']\nP: Animation architecture: data model, parallel evaluation pipeline, animation/physics/gameplay sync and root-motion policy, animation LOD, budgets.\nNR: [['Sampling and blending', 'animation-runtime'], ['Skinning', 'deformation-skinning']]\nprov ['C-ANIM'] cons ['C-ECS', 'C-SPATIAL', 'C-FRAME', 'C-TASK', 'C-PHYS?']\n##### network-transport ['online', 'server']\nP: UDP sockets and platform network APIs, reliability and ordering, fragmentation, congestion control, encryption and authentication, NAT traversal and relays, connection lifecycle, link simulation, QUIC/WebTransport evaluation.\nNR: [['What is replicated', 'replication'], ['Relay service operation', 'platform-online-services']]\nprov [] cons ['C-PAL', 'C-TASK', 'C-SVC?']\n##### dedicated-server ['online', 'server']\nP: Headless server builds and stripping, tick cost and multi-instance density, fleet orchestration boundary, server observability, listen servers and host migration.\nNR: [['Fleet operation (outside engine scope)', 'platform-online-services'], ['Server logging substrate', 'observability-telemetry']]\nprov [] cons ['C-NET', 'C-FRAME', 'C-SVC']\n##### scripting-runtime ['all']\nP: Scripting language selection, VM embedding and bindings, sandboxing, debugging and profiling, hot reload, visual scripting, AOT/JIT constraints, GC policy.\nNR: [['Reflection substrate', 'reflection-metadata'], ['Graph editor UI', 'graph-editor-framework']]\nprov ['C-SCRIPT'] cons ['C-REFL', 'C-GAME', 'C-RELOAD']\n##### visual-debugging-tools ['all']\nP: Debug draw API, in-game console and cheats, runtime entity inspector and gameplay debugger, visual logger and rewind, debug menus and overlays.\nNR: [['Logging and traces', 'observability-telemetry'], ['Render buffer visualization', 'render-architect']]\nprov [] cons ['C-INSTR', 'C-ECS', 'C-DRAW2D?', 'C-RSCENE?', 'C-DET?']","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"e933c5e4-218c-4e50-a0cc-4b389265676f","timestamp":"2026-09-29T15:46:42.494Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e139c989-20d9-42eb-8634-3c2f4bd176a0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"remote_mobile","cwd":"/home/user/skills","sessionId":"64f15158-6a4e-5bdf-8a90-7f2bd7b05b82","version":"2.1.284","gitBranch":"claude/engine-skill-framework-phase1"}
